name atomic-10x-tuples
# Every line is one object. Its members "head", "relation" and "tail" are the tuple, in that order, each as written:
# [head, relation, tail], which the set attests, scored by "p_valid_model", the number between 0 and 1 its critic gives
# every tuple. "rec_0.5" .. "rec_0.9" are that same number against thresholds (each true where p_valid_model is at least
# 0.65344 / 0.83781 / 0.92709 / 0.95577 / 0.96755, checked on 1M lines), and "split" is which part of the release a line
# is in: neither says anything of the tuple, and neither is read.
match ATOMIC10X.jsonl
format json
tier record by \n

thing record head relation tail
content head relation tail p_valid_model
omit split rec_*
itself record
score record p_valid_model
